Negative control for the replay treatment's colour family (`H2` · `AC2.8`).

Repaints the rail's played half — indicator and connector — in the warning
family and changes nothing else: the same stops, the same done · current ·
pending states, the same seek. So the only claim that can go red is the ruled
one: a playing scenario is the primary family, and warning stays reserved for
actual warnings.

Re-targeted 2026-08-13 after `R7-8` gave the rail its own row and dropped the
bar-scale overrides the old hunk's context carried. Same claim, same red,
current source.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the replay-treatment case — the rail carries nothing from the warning
family in either of its played states.

